THOUGHT: Changing the field to @Nullable fixed the FIELD_NO_INIT error but introduced new dereference and return-type errors. The logic guarantees color is non-null during update (begin() sets it, and TemporalAction ensures begin runs before update), and getColor is documented to return null. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I’ll (1) add a local non-null variable in update() after asserting color is non-null, and (2) annotate getColor’s return type as @Nullable. Then I’ll rebuild to confirm the total error count drops from 286 to 283 (284 original − 1 fixed + 0 new).

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '39,42c\  protected void update(float percent) {
    if (color == null) throw new IllegalStateException("color must not be null in update()");
    Color c = color;
    if (percent == 0) c.a = start;
    else if (percent == 1) c.a = end;
    else c.a = start + (end - start) * percent;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/actions/AlphaAction.java && sed -i '50s/public @Null Color/public @javax.annotation.Nullable Color/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/actions/AlphaAction.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -Eo '[0-9]+ errors' initial_build_output.log | tail -n 1 && grep -Eo '[0-9]+ errors' new_build_output.log | tail -n 1 && grep -n "AlphaAction" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

